# MINIMUM signing dependencies for the release-signing job (Step 1L).
#
# The signing runner is the only place the release seed exists, so it
# installs the smallest possible dependency set: the narrow
# `release_pipeline.py sign-manifest` command needs the Ed25519 primitives
# from `cryptography` and nothing else. The build
# toolchain (build/twine/setuptools) is deliberately NOT here — building
# happens on a separate runner that never sees the seed.
#
# Locked for Ubuntu 24.04 / CPython 3.12.3, the exact runner and interpreter
# selectors used by the workflow.
# Regenerate ONLY inside a clean Linux environment:
#
#   python3.12 -m venv /tmp/olymp-signing-lock
#   /tmp/olymp-signing-lock/bin/python --version  # Python 3.12.3
#   /tmp/olymp-signing-lock/bin/pip install 'pip==24.0' 'pip-tools==7.6.1'
#   /tmp/olymp-signing-lock/bin/pip-compile --generate-hashes --allow-unsafe \
#       --strip-extras --output-file=requirements-signing.lock \
#       requirements-signing.in
#
# The toolchain is pinned so the lock is reproducible: an unpinned
# pip/pip-tools would change resolution or output formatting between runs and
# the byte-identity check would fail for a reason unrelated to the inputs.
#
pip==24.0
cryptography
